/* Usage descriptions for the camera and microphone (design-l2 §10.6). The English values must stay byte-identical to ElderlyAssistant/Info.plist; L10nCatalogCoverageTests pins the equality. */

"NSCameraUsageDescription" = "The camera is used to verify medication intake, to photograph appliances, remotes, or screens when you ask for help using them, and to take an ordinary photo when you ask for one — that photo is then saved to your photo library. The camera is also used to read printed text aloud in your language with live translation. Appliance photos are sent to the assistant's cloud service so it can guide you. For live translation, only the text seen by the camera is sent — and only when the phone's own dictionary cannot translate it. Photos of that text are never sent. When you tap \"what is this?\", the small picture of the tapped thing — only that picture, and nothing else from your camera — is sent to the assistant's cloud service to work out what it is. The camera can also record a short instruction video for a reminder; that video stays on this phone and is never uploaded or shared.";
"NSMicrophoneUsageDescription" = "The assistant needs microphone access to hear your voice commands. By default your speech goes to Gemini, a cloud service, to be turned into text — you can switch to a fully on-device engine in Settings → Voice Engine. The microphone is also used to record the sound in a short instruction video for a reminder; that recording stays on this phone and is never uploaded or shared.";
